# Secrets — the Groq key and DB URL live here
# Secrets. The bare `.env` rule this replaces matched ONLY the exact name, so
# .env.local / .env.production / .env.staging were all one `git add -A` away
# from being published. Ignore the whole family, then re-admit the two that are
# deliberately public: .env.example is a template, .env.test is localhost and a
# fake secret and exists so anyone can run the suite.
.env*
!.env.example
!.env.test

